{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1349194-trying-to-find-a-creature-from-first-or-second-edition","id":1349194,"title":"Trying to find a creature from first or second edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-17T16:39:12-08:00","id":1349194,"title":"Trying to find a creature from first or second edition","content":"It was a species of giant birds with human faces, native to Nexus. They could mimic human voices, and were known to kidnap children. I can\u2019t remember the name of the creature, nor which book it was printed in. I remember there was art of this creature, showing it swooping down to attack someone. <br /> <br /> Can anyone point me to the source, and if possible, let me know if it has updated stats yet in 3rd edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> This one is for all my Exigents...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/102-lordwyrmsbane","name":"LordWyrmsBane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T16:48:07-08:00","id":1349197,"title":"","content":"You're thinking of the Karmeus. The 1e writeup is in <i>Creatures of the Wyld</i>, page 118. I believe the 2e writeup to be in <i>the Compass of Terrestrial Directions Vol. I - The Scavenger Lands.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T16:54:22-08:00","id":1349200,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure there's no statblock for them in 3e, though there ARE Wyld-birds and talking birds and such in Hundred Devils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:19:50-08:00","id":1349228,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar97_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"97\" data-vbnamecard=\"97\">The MG</a> is right on both counts.<br /> <br /> Though one note for the OP: They don\u2019t kidnap children - they prey on them. That\u2019s kind of an important distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:57:55-08:00","id":1349265,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.c